{"n": 1244, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "1244.webp", "text": "Condition\n\nCrackle and sizzle\n\nCrackle and knock\n\nHow! and/or whistle, depending on engine speed\n\nSizzle and knock\n\nKnock and crash\n\nHowl and crackle\n\nScale light not on, no reception\n\nScale light on, no background noise with loudness\ncontrol turned up fully; automatic station tuner\nmalfunctions\n\n65-119\n\nTROUBLESHOOTING\n\nPossible Cause\n\nTune in a weak station just next to the station concerned. Accelerate engine to about 5,000 rpm, turn off ignition.\nRadio should still be receiving. If reception noise disappears when turning off ignition, ignition disturbance is concerned.\nCHECK:\n\n— Shielding of distributor cap.\n\n— Shielding ground wire connection.\n\n— Shielding capacitor 2.2 pF at ignition coil term, (15),\n\nIMPORTANT! Not for thyristor ignition,\n\nShielded filter in wire (1).\n\nPerfect connection and resistance of ignition wires - plug caps/distributor cap/ignition coil.\n\nDistributor rotor resistance*.\n\nHairline cracks in distributor cap/distributor rotor/plug caps/spark Plugs/ignition coil neck.\n\nGround wire of engine/firewall )\n\nGround wire of engine hood/body ) perfect contact\n\nGround connection of radio )\n\nEngine hood closed correctly.\n\nAccelerate engine until interference noise is considerably louder. Now turn on headlights and rear window defogger.\nIf noise disappears or changes, regulator is defective.\n\nDetach drive belts and run engine briefly. If this eliminates the interfergnce, check capacitor at term. (+) on the\nalternator. If an electronic antenna is installed, install a 2.2 pF bypassing, capacitor in the positive wire to the electronic\nantenna (at antenna height) as close as possible to the wire inlet of the anténna amplifier.\n\nThis interference is only heard while driving and disappears when operating thegrake pedal.\nCause — electrostatic charge.\nRemedy — install wheel hub contacts on front axle.\n\nThese noises are similar to those for ignition disturbances and are caused by a break in the antenna wire (usually occurs\nwhile driving).\n\nThis interference will disappear when switching off extra equipment, for example:\nWindshield wiper motor }\n\nWasher pump ) remedy: install shielded filter 2 x 0.47 pF\n\nExtra fan )\n\n— Fuse oxidation\n\n— Fuse defective - type*\n\n— Power wire loose/not connected\n— Ground connection\n\nRadio defective\n\nSpeaker wire plug loose on radio\n\nBreak in speaker wires\n\nPlugs on speaker balance control loose\nSpeakers defective\n\nDummy plug on tape socket loose or defective\n~ Radio defective\n\n* See Specifications", "words": [["Condition", 0.0218, 0.1207, 0.0719, 0.132], ["Crackle", 0.0218, 0.1525, 0.0598, 0.1645], ["and", 0.0628, 0.1532, 0.0795, 0.1638], ["sizzle", 0.0836, 0.1532, 0.1079, 0.1638], ["Crackle", 0.0223, 0.4098, 0.0598, 0.4218], ["and", 0.0628, 0.4105, 0.08, 0.4218], ["knock", 0.0836, 0.4105, 0.1114, 0.4218], ["How!", 0.0228, 0.4589, 0.0486, 0.4702], ["and/or", 0.0522, 0.4589, 0.0841, 0.4702], ["whistle,", 0.0871, 0.4595, 0.1226, 0.4721], ["depending", 0.1261, 0.4595, 0.1753, 0.4735], ["on", 0.1778, 0.4629, 0.19, 0.4708], ["engine", 0.1935, 0.4602, 0.2244, 0.4735], ["speed", 0.2275, 0.4602, 0.2543, 0.4728], ["Sizzle", 0.0218, 0.5225, 0.0512, 0.5345], ["and", 0.0542, 0.5239, 0.0719, 0.5345], ["knock", 0.075, 0.5232, 0.1033, 0.5345], ["Knock", 0.0228, 0.5875, 0.0547, 0.5988], ["and", 0.0572, 0.5849, 0.0735, 0.6054], ["crash", 0.078, 0.5849, 0.1049, 0.6054], ["Howl", 0.0223, 0.6359, 0.0486, 0.6466], ["and", 0.0517, 0.6366, 0.0694, 0.6466], ["crackle", 0.0724, 0.6359, 0.1059, 0.6472], ["Scale", 0.0218, 0.7162, 0.0476, 0.7275], ["light", 0.0517, 0.7162, 0.0724, 0.7294], ["not", 0.076, 0.7182, 0.0912, 0.7275], ["on,", 0.0947, 0.7195, 0.1094, 0.7288], ["no", 0.113, 0.7195, 0.1241, 0.7275], ["reception", 0.1277, 0.7168, 0.1722, 0.7294], ["Scale", 0.0213, 0.813, 0.0471, 0.8243], ["light", 0.0517, 0.8137, 0.0724, 0.8263], ["on,", 0.0755, 0.8163, 0.09